  "findings": [
    "The deficiency criterion proves self-adjointness of the actual closed densely defined symmetric operator by orthogonal graph projection; neither resolvent surjectivity nor a self-adjoint extension is assumed.",
    "Closure identities use closability from symmetry and actual equality of adjoints before applying the two-deficiency criterion.",
    "For the invariant norm-preserving real group, the deficiency pairing obeys f'=ca f and is bounded for ALL real t. Nonzero c and deficiency eigenvalue force f=0. Negative t is genuinely part of the hypothesis.",
    "The concrete Segal consumer supplies density, symmetry, Weyl domain invariance and derivative from the previously constructed canonical Fock objects. Colinear CCR phase vanishes, giving a genuine one-parameter group; c=sqrt(2) is nonzero.",
    "The conclusion is essential self-adjointness of segal f on its original exponential domain and closedness of its closure, with that domain as core."
